usage: main [-h] [--version] [--fastq FASTQ] [--k K] [--w W] [--xmin XMIN]
            [--xmax XMAX] [--T T] [--exact] [--disable_numpy]
            [--delta_len DELTA_LEN] [--max_seqs_to_spoa MAX_SEQS_TO_SPOA]
            [--max_seqs MAX_SEQS]
            [--exact_instance_limit EXACT_INSTANCE_LIMIT]
            [--set_w_dynamically] [--verbose] [--compression]
            [--outfolder OUTFOLDER] [--delta_iso_len_3 DELTA_ISO_LEN_3]
            [--delta_iso_len_5 DELTA_ISO_LEN_5] [--parallel PARALLEL] [--slow]

De novo error correction of long-read transcriptome reads

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  --fastq FASTQ         Path to input fastq file with reads (default: False)
  --k K                 Kmer size (default: 20)
  --w W                 Window size (default: 31)
  --xmin XMIN           Upper interval length (default: 18)
  --xmax XMAX           Lower interval length (default: 80)
  --T T                 Minimum fraction keeping substitution (default: 0.1)
  --exact               Get exact solution for WIS for every read
                        (recalculating weights for each read (much slower but
                        slightly more accuracy, not to be used for clusters
                        with over ~500 reads) (default: False)
  --disable_numpy       Do not require numpy to be installed, but this version
                        is about 1.5x slower than with numpy. (default: False)
  --delta_len DELTA_LEN
                        Maximum length difference between two reads intervals
                        for which they would still be merged (default: 5)
  --max_seqs_to_spoa MAX_SEQS_TO_SPOA
                        Maximum number of seqs to spoa (default: 200)
  --max_seqs MAX_SEQS   Maximum number of seqs to correct at a time (in case
                        of large clusters). (default: 1000)
  --exact_instance_limit EXACT_INSTANCE_LIMIT
                        Activates slower exact mode for instance smaller than
                        this limit (default: 0)
  --set_w_dynamically   Set w = k + max(2*k, floor(cluster_size/1000)).
                        (default: False)
  --verbose             Print various developer stats. (default: False)
  --compression         Use homopolymer compressed reads. (Deprecated, because
                        we will have fewer minmimizer combinations to span
                        regions in homopolymenr dense regions. Solution could
                        be to adjust upper interval length dynamically to
                        guarantee a certain number of spanning intervals.
                        (default: False)
  --outfolder OUTFOLDER
                        The outfolder of isONform, into which the algorithm
                        will write the results. (default: None)
  --delta_iso_len_3 DELTA_ISO_LEN_3
                        Cutoff parameter: maximum length difference at 3prime
                        end, for which subisoforms are still merged into
                        longer isoforms (default: 30)
  --delta_iso_len_5 DELTA_ISO_LEN_5
                        Cutoff parameter: maximum length difference at 5prime
                        end, for which subisoforms are still merged into
                        longer isoforms (default: 50)
  --parallel PARALLEL   Indicates whether we run the parallelization wrapper
                        script (default: False)
  --slow                EXPERIMENTAL PARAMETER: has high repercussions on run
                        time use the slow mode for the simplification of the
                        graph (bubble popping), slow mode: every bubble gets
                        popped. (default: False)
